  "brief": "C.H. Robinson to acquire freight broker RXO in a $5.8 billion deal, expanding its logistics capabilities.\n\nC.H. Robinson / RXO (Announced): C.H. Robinson to buy RXO. C.H. Robinson is acquiring freight broker RXO in a $5.8 billion deal [2, 5, 6]. The acquisition is expected to expand C.H. Robinson's logistics capabilities [2, 5, 6]. The deal has been announced and is currently under review [1, 2, 3].\nSchneider Electric / PTC (Announced): Schneider Electric to Acquire PTC. Schneider Electric is acquiring PTC in a $22.6 billion deal [9, 10, 12]. The acquisition is expected to boost industrial intelligence [11, 14]. The deal will be paid in cash [13, 15, 16].\nCuraleaf / Aurora Cannabis (Announced): Curaleaf and Aurora Cannabis Deal. Curaleaf is acquiring Aurora Cannabis [21, 22, 23]. The deal was sweetened to $5 a share [20, 21, 26]. The offer was increased by 25% [24]. The deal was announced [27].\nCenovus / Athabasca Oil (Announced): Cenovus to Acquire Athabasca Oil. Cenovus Energy is acquiring Athabasca Oil in a $4 billion deal [29, 31, 34]. The deal is valued at $4 billion [29, 31, 34]. Cenovus Energy will acquire Athabasca Oil [29, 31, 34].\nMcKesson / Option Care Health (Rumored): McKesson to Buy Option Care Health. McKesson is reportedly considering a $5 billion-plus deal to buy Option Care Health [36, 37, 38]. The deal is rumored to be near completion, with CD&R reportedly involved [36, 37, 38]. No official announcement has been made, but the deal is expected to be confirmed soon [36, 37, 38].\niRhythm / VitalConnect (Announced): iRhythm and VitalConnect Deal. iRhythm acquires VitalConnect in a $237.5M deal [39, 40]. The deal is expected to bring revenue growth and a 15% adjusted EBITDA target for 2027 [40]. The acquisition was announced on October 5 [39].\nOpenAI / UAE funds (Rumored): OpenAI and UAE funds. OpenAI is in talks with UAE funds to secure a $30 billion funding round [41, 42]. The deal is still in the early stages and no further details have been announced [41, 42].\nMFN Partners / RXO (Announced): MFN Partners and RXO Deal. MFN Partners and RXO have signed a voting pact with a 19.3% stake [43, 3, 4]. C.H. Robinson is acquiring RXO in a $5.8 billion deal [8, 6, 5]. The deal stage is announced, but no further details have been released [3, 4, 6].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- Fathom and Bed Bath and Beyond terminate merger [44].\n- Electronic Arts Bondholders Allege Default Following Largest LBO [45].\n- Basware Finalises Trustpair Acquisition to Combat Global Payment Fraud [46].",
